- I'll cut off my right hand. - Fine.

280
00:23:00,921 --> 00:23:03,924
Let's find out. Darn, you're losing that hand today.

281
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:06,635
- At least he's a good kid. - He really is.

282
00:23:07,261 --> 00:23:09,053
- Do it. - Let's see.

283
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,388
- I'm opening it. - As if.

284
00:23:10,389 --> 00:23:11,473
- Jeez. - I'm opening it.

285
00:23:12,016 --> 00:23:13,850
- No way. - Seriously?

286
00:23:13,851 --> 00:23:16,311
- See? I told you, morons! - What the?

287
00:23:16,312 --> 00:23:17,937
Hey, look for the key.

288
00:23:17,938 --> 00:23:19,564
- Here it is. - It's here!

289
00:23:19,565 --> 00:23:21,942
- I told you it was ditched. - Sweet!

290
00:23:22,985 --> 00:23:25,613
All right, let's see what this car can do!

291
00:23:27,531 --> 00:23:29,158
Step on it!

292
00:23:30,159 --> 00:23:31,744
It's darn fast.

293
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,127
- Great! - Oh, jeez.

294
00:23:41,003 --> 00:23:43,671
This is sick.

295
00:23:43,672 --> 00:23:44,964
- Isn't this great? - Darn.

296
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:46,633
- Wait, guys. - What is it?

297
00:23:46,634 --> 00:23:48,551
Darn, the cops are on our tail.

298
00:23:48,552 --> 00:23:50,679
Man, it's the cops.

299
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:52,889
See? I told you this car was sketchy.

300
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:55,266
It's because you turned this up so loud.

301
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:56,976
Does that even matter? I said this car...

302
00:23:56,977 --> 00:23:58,019
Knock it off.

303
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:00,104
Pull the car over first.

304
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:02,483
- Pull over. - Fine, I'm pulling over.

305
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:10,365
- Detective. - What?

306
00:24:10,366 --> 00:24:13,076
I'm dead serious. The key was right there in the car.

307
00:24:13,077 --> 00:24:14,703
- The key was inside? - Yes.

308
00:24:15,287 --> 00:24:17,580
And the headlight was already broken.

309
00:24:17,581 --> 00:24:18,748
The bumper and grille too?

310
00:24:18,749 --> 00:24:20,625
Right, and when we looked at it closely,

311
00:24:20,626 --> 00:24:23,712
the car was badly damaged, and the color was, like, poop brown.

312
00:24:24,296 --> 00:24:25,296
So we naturally figured...

313
00:24:25,297 --> 00:24:27,090
it was abandoned, which is why we took it.

314
00:24:27,091 --> 00:24:28,801
- True. - Right.

315
00:24:32,805 --> 00:24:34,681
- Hold on a second, Detective. - What?

316
00:24:34,682 --> 00:24:36,933
Maybe the owner caused an accident and ditched the car...

317
00:24:36,934 --> 00:24:38,393
to avoid getting busted.

318
00:24:38,394 --> 00:24:40,561
Exactly. Why would anyone ditch such an expensive car?

319
00:24:40,562 --> 00:24:42,355
- I told you it was sketchy. - It adds up.

320
00:24:42,356 --> 00:24:44,984
- Makes sense. Maybe this guy killed someone. - Hey.

321
00:24:45,484 --> 00:24:46,610
Sit down.

322
00:24:48,570 --> 00:24:52,198
I'm telling you, this guy murdered someone.

323
00:24:52,199 --> 00:24:53,783
We've got to grill them hard.

324
00:24:53,784 --> 00:24:54,951
Boys.

325
00:24:54,952 --> 00:24:56,536
Be quiet.

326
00:24:56,537 --> 00:24:57,912
- Okay? - Yes, sir.

327
00:24:57,913 --> 00:24:58,998
Yes, sir.

328
00:24:59,790 --> 00:25:02,375
So, the headlight was already smashed?

329
00:25:02,376 --> 00:25:03,669
- Yes. - Yes.

330
00:25:51,216 --> 00:25:53,052
Min Seo.

331
00:25:59,016 --> 00:26:02,436
Are you using protection properly?

332
00:26:03,479 --> 00:26:07,816
I think it's all just curiosity.

333
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:10,486
A passing phase.

334
00:26:11,278 --> 00:26:14,614
Does she actually love you?

335
00:26:14,615 --> 00:26:16,658
Can you even trust her?

336
00:26:17,701 --> 00:26:20,662
Oh, men are all the same.

337
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,040
Love is...

338
00:26:23,707 --> 00:26:25,751
- pointless. - How much did she drink?

339
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:28,170
I'm serious.

340
00:26:29,421 --> 00:26:31,090
Min Seo.

341
00:26:33,550 --> 00:26:35,010
I mean it.

342
00:26:38,263 --> 00:26:40,808
Do you still visit your dad's house?

343
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:46,396
Min Seo, you can't ever leave me.

344
00:26:47,356 --> 00:26:51,652
You're all I have left now, okay?

345
00:26:52,778 --> 00:26:57,908
I'll do whatever it takes to keep you safe.

346
00:26:59,743 --> 00:27:01,203
No matter what.

347
00:27:02,538 --> 00:27:04,497
Min Seo, I love you.

348
00:27:04,498 --> 00:27:06,291
What is she even saying?

349
00:27:22,141 --> 00:27:24,268
Dad, why are you lying there?

350
00:27:29,064 --> 00:27:30,858
Oh, Ye Ji.

351
00:28:15,444 --> 00:28:18,029
I'll do it, Dad. Just sit down.

352
00:28:18,030 --> 00:28:20,282
No, Ye Ji. I need to do this.

353
00:28:46,850 --> 00:28:47,976
Lim Ye Ji.

354
00:28:50,354 --> 00:28:51,521
Yes, Mother.

355
00:28:52,439 --> 00:28:53,941
Are you sure...

356
00:28:54,441 --> 00:28:56,443
Min Seo feels the same way about you?

357
00:29:00,113 --> 00:29:01,198
Then,

358
00:29:01,907 --> 00:29:03,617
why would she shift the blame onto you?

359
00:29:09,957 --> 00:29:11,291
Answer her.

360
00:29:12,668 --> 00:29:14,418
Even after promising to love you for life...

361
00:29:14,419 --> 00:29:17,088
and stay by your side until old age,

362
00:29:17,089 --> 00:29:19,007
people can still betray you.

363
00:29:21,343 --> 00:29:23,886
She's right, Ye Ji. It'd be best if you two...

364
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:26,181
- broke up as soon as... - Which is why...

365
00:29:28,058 --> 00:29:30,602
you've got to become stronger at a time like this.

366
00:29:31,770 --> 00:29:33,855
You went so far as to cover for her.

367
00:29:34,940 --> 00:29:37,693
It'll be too unfair if she betrays you.

368
00:29:39,319 --> 00:29:40,445
Do you get...

369
00:29:41,321 --> 00:29:42,489
what I'm saying?

370
00:29:45,617 --> 00:29:47,744
Right, don't break up.

371
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:51,915
You've got to stick together when things get tough.

372
00:29:53,333 --> 00:29:56,544
Let's take this as a chance for our own family too.

373
00:29:56,545 --> 00:29:57,713
Right, Ye Ji?

374
00:29:58,547 --> 00:30:01,216
So that our family can become stronger,

375
00:30:02,134 --> 00:30:03,969
I'll do my best, honey.

376
00:30:06,972 --> 00:30:08,514
Both my husband and kid...

377
00:30:08,515 --> 00:30:10,955
Are they all under some spell from the women across the road?

378
00:30:14,563 --> 00:30:16,773
Oh, I'm getting a call.

379
00:30:18,150 --> 00:30:19,735
It's an unknown number.

380
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:22,529
Let me grab this real quick. One moment.

381
00:30:26,033 --> 00:30:27,534
Cha Eun Bin, speaking.

382
00:30:29,578 --> 00:30:32,039
Oh, yes. I'm Lim Jae Hong.

383
00:30:33,332 --> 00:30:34,750
The police?

384
00:30:46,887 --> 00:30:48,847
Are you really not going to press charges?

385
00:30:49,723 --> 00:30:51,015
No.

386
00:30:51,016 --> 00:30:52,933
I just want to settle this quietly.

387
00:30:52,934 --> 00:30:56,354
- Get inside already. Move. - We'll talk inside.

388
00:30:56,355 --> 00:30:59,941
Those guys are habitual offenders. Forgiveness won't change them.

389
00:31:00,442 --> 00:31:03,195
They caused an accident themselves and lied about it.

390
00:31:03,987 --> 00:31:07,740
You've got to slap people like that with a huge repair bill.

391
00:31:07,741 --> 00:31:10,409
I mean, even that won't change them.

392
00:31:10,410 --> 00:31:11,411
Well, it seems...

393
00:31:12,329 --> 00:31:14,539
they're still young.

394
00:31:16,166 --> 00:31:18,835
People make mistakes in life.

395
00:31:20,337 --> 00:31:22,631
Shouldn't we give them a second chance?

396
00:31:23,799 --> 00:31:25,300
I guess so.

397
00:31:28,011 --> 00:31:30,346
Hi, honey. I handled it well.

398
00:31:30,347 --> 00:31:31,931
- Are you sure? - Yes.

399
00:31:31,932 --> 00:31:33,933
You didn't get nervous and slip up, did you?

400
00:31:33,934 --> 00:31:36,561
I was hardly nervous.

401
00:31:38,563 --> 00:31:40,941
I was slightly anxious at first,

402
00:31:41,525 --> 00:31:44,360
but I completely immersed myself in method acting.

403
00:31:44,361 --> 00:31:47,696
I did my magic, and the cop bought it right away.

404
00:31:47,697 --> 00:31:48,949
- Did he? - Yes.

405
00:31:49,866 --> 00:31:52,785
Besides, those thugs...

406
00:31:52,786 --> 00:31:54,745
had a ton of similar offenses.

407
00:31:54,746 --> 00:31:56,080
- Offenses? - Yes.

408
00:31:56,081 --> 00:31:57,498
- So, it's all taken care of? - Yes.

409
00:31:57,499 --> 00:31:58,792
- Okay, bye. - What?

410
00:32:17,310 --> 00:32:19,521
Hello, Mr. Sol. Long time no see, sir.

411
00:32:21,022 --> 00:32:23,150
- Jeez. - Great! I got it.

412
00:32:25,735 --> 00:32:27,779
Why is it so hard to win?

413
00:32:30,782 --> 00:32:33,034
Well, grab a seat somewhere.

414
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:35,662
Did my brother, Sol, not come by here?

415
00:32:37,581 --> 00:32:40,834
Oh, you're Mr. Do, sir. Hello.

416
00:32:42,002 --> 00:32:44,588
After causing that commotion last time...

417
00:32:45,505 --> 00:32:48,425
Anyway, he hasn't been anywhere near here since then.

418
00:32:51,678 --> 00:32:53,929
Give me a call if he shows up.

419
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:55,640
Yes, sir.

420
00:33:00,145 --> 00:33:01,396
What...

421
00:33:01,688 --> 00:33:03,190
What is it?

422
00:33:05,108 --> 00:33:06,817
You don't know my number.

423
00:33:06,818 --> 00:33:08,819
- Oh, right. - Give me a call, okay?

424
00:33:08,820 --> 00:33:11,072
Yes, sir. Goodbye.

425
00:33:11,865 --> 00:33:14,867
I dug through every branch nationwide to find this.

426
00:33:14,868 --> 00:33:17,913
Do the legwork yourself for the details.

427
00:33:18,371 --> 00:33:20,164
So, I'm actually...

428
00:33:20,165 --> 00:33:23,167
in urgent need of tracking down a car from an accident, sir.

429
00:33:23,168 --> 00:33:24,877
Do you mind if I ask...

430
00:33:24,878 --> 00:33:27,214
about the condition of this one?

431
00:33:28,256 --> 00:33:29,716
- This car? - Yes.

432
00:33:31,510 --> 00:33:33,386
This car...

433
00:33:35,805 --> 00:33:38,557
It's just in the shop...

434
00:33:38,558 --> 00:33:40,101
for some internal repairs.

435
00:33:41,478 --> 00:33:43,812
Any smashed or broken parts...

436
00:33:43,813 --> 00:33:45,648
on the front end?

437
00:33:45,649 --> 00:33:47,525
No, it simply needs...

438
00:33:47,526 --> 00:33:49,528
a fan belt replacement.

439
00:33:54,157 --> 00:33:55,909
Sir, I'm kind of in a rush here.

440
00:34:03,542 --> 00:34:05,709
(Imported Car Repair, Cheongnam Motors)

441
00:34:05,710 --> 00:34:10,381
(Go-to for domestic SUVs)

442
00:34:10,382 --> 00:34:12,842
(Exclusive repair shop for rich-gold-limited-edition owners)

443
00:34:16,304 --> 00:34:17,680
What the?

444
00:34:17,681 --> 00:34:19,307
Why are they all so far away?

445
00:34:19,474 --> 00:34:21,058
(Busan)

446
00:34:21,059 --> 00:34:22,852
(CN First Motors, Cheongnam Motors)

447
00:34:28,483 --> 00:34:30,193
(Dr. Ahn off for the morning)

448
00:34:31,194 --> 00:34:32,570
- Hello. - Hello.

449
00:34:32,571 --> 00:34:33,696
Today, Dr. Ahn is...

450
00:34:33,697 --> 00:34:35,739
Dr. Ahn is out today?

451
00:34:35,740 --> 00:34:37,074
All of a sudden?

452
00:34:37,075 --> 00:34:39,243
You should've notified me in advance.

453
00:34:39,244 --> 00:34:40,494
I'm so sorry.

454
00:34:40,495 --> 00:34:42,914
A seminar was scheduled at the last minute.

455
00:34:44,291 --> 00:34:45,499
If it's okay,

456
00:34:45,500 --> 00:34:48,419
would you mind seeing another doctor today?

457
00:34:48,420 --> 00:34:50,629
Forget it. I'll come back another time.

458
00:34:50,630 --> 00:34:52,673
- Goodness. - Apologies.

459
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:54,050
Goodbye.

460
00:35:16,865 --> 00:35:19,625
We're in the middle of the investment review. What were you thinking?

461
00:35:20,243 --> 00:35:21,244
Tell me.

462
00:35:22,078 --> 00:35:23,663
Where exactly did you...

463
00:35:24,539 --> 00:35:26,124
spend 300 million won?

464
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:31,046
I need to know the details so we can get our stories straight.

465
00:35:32,255 --> 00:35:33,548
Captain Park.

466
00:35:34,674 --> 00:35:36,301
What's going on?

467
00:35:37,260 --> 00:35:38,595
What happened is...

468
00:35:40,221 --> 00:35:41,348
No, nothing.

469
00:35:42,182 --> 00:35:44,850
I'll put it back in a few days.

470
00:35:44,851 --> 00:35:47,854
I'll fix this so fast they won't even realize it was gone.

471
00:35:53,818 --> 00:35:55,278
Oh, my.

472
00:35:56,196 --> 00:35:58,073
What do I do?

473
00:35:59,449 --> 00:36:00,450
Seriously...

474
00:36:03,620 --> 00:36:05,246
Are you okay? I'm sorry.

475
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:09,584
There's no one around, and they still put a speed bump here.

476
00:36:10,085 --> 00:36:11,670
Oh, goodness.

477
00:36:14,589 --> 00:36:17,300
I'm so messed up.

478
00:36:35,694 --> 00:36:37,653
That's absurd.

479
00:36:37,654 --> 00:36:39,698
If you get caught, that's embezzlement...

480
00:36:43,785 --> 00:36:44,828
Gosh.

481
00:36:45,995 --> 00:36:47,622
Hello, Dr. Joo.

482
00:36:48,581 --> 00:36:49,624
Yes.

483
00:36:51,292 --> 00:36:53,460
Hi, I'm calling because...

484
00:36:53,461 --> 00:36:55,588
today's our first meeting, right?

485
00:36:56,589 --> 00:36:58,590
It seems like the perfect time...

486
00:36:58,591 --> 00:37:00,802
for your team to get a sugar boost.

487
00:37:01,720 --> 00:37:02,721
Yes.

488
00:37:03,304 --> 00:37:06,557
And I've arrived a little early.

489
00:37:06,558 --> 00:37:07,766
Do you mind if I go up?

490
00:37:07,767 --> 00:37:08,767
(No eating in the office)

491
00:37:08,768 --> 00:37:09,978
Of course, Dr. Joo.

492
00:37:22,991 --> 00:37:24,993
Darn it.

493
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:34,335
I'm here to sort out...

494
00:37:34,961 --> 00:37:37,672
what happened yesterday as quickly as possible.

495
00:37:42,677 --> 00:37:44,261
Here.

496
00:37:44,262 --> 00:37:46,138
It's the 151 million won.

497
00:37:46,139 --> 00:37:48,141
How dare you show up here?

498
00:37:54,397 --> 00:37:56,191
Ms. Park.

499
00:38:12,624 --> 00:38:14,374
Good grief, I...

500
00:38:14,375 --> 00:38:16,294
I'm truly sorry.

501
00:38:17,212 --> 00:38:18,837
I won't make any excuses.

502
00:38:18,838 --> 00:38:21,715
I don't know what I was thinking.

503
00:38:21,716 --> 00:38:24,968
It really was a mistake,

504
00:38:24,969 --> 00:38:28,139
and I swear I'll never see him again.

505
00:38:33,853 --> 00:38:36,564
For the sake of Ye Ji and Min Seo,

506
00:38:37,315 --> 00:38:38,650
let's...

507
00:38:39,651 --> 00:38:42,403
Let's please pretend nothing happened,

508
00:38:42,946 --> 00:38:44,905
including that video,

509
00:38:44,906 --> 00:38:45,949
and go back to being...

510
00:38:46,533 --> 00:38:47,534
Oh, my.

511
00:38:50,078 --> 00:38:51,912
Get the heck out...

512
00:38:51,913 --> 00:38:53,832
before I completely humiliate you.

513
00:39:03,550 --> 00:39:04,926
Jeez.

514
00:39:05,468 --> 00:39:06,970
This is driving me nuts.

515
00:39:21,317 --> 00:39:23,235
Thank you so much...

516
00:39:23,236 --> 00:39:25,571
- for the autograph. - My pleasure.

517
00:39:25,572 --> 00:39:28,073
Oh, I've been really enjoying your work...

518
00:39:28,074 --> 00:39:29,825
- on "Model House." - I see.

519
00:39:29,826 --> 00:39:31,368
It's quite entertaining.

520
00:39:31,369 --> 00:39:32,786
It's "Townhouse," actually.

521
00:39:32,787 --> 00:39:35,330
Model or town, it makes no difference.

522
00:39:35,331 --> 00:39:37,040
A house is a house, right?

523
00:39:37,041 --> 00:39:38,041
Right.

524
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:40,043
Anyway, you're so handsome.

525
00:39:40,044 --> 00:39:43,130
How long is it going to take to fix?

526
00:39:43,131 --> 00:39:45,632
I'll do it as soon as possible and hit you up when it's ready.

527
00:39:45,633 --> 00:39:47,426
All right.

528
00:39:47,427 --> 00:39:49,136
- I'll take off, then. - Sure.

529
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:50,762
- My cab is here. - I see.

530
00:39:50,763 --> 00:39:52,097
Thank you. Take good care of it.

531
00:39:52,098 --> 00:39:53,558
- Bye. - Bye.

532
00:39:54,392 --> 00:39:55,767
Goodness.

533
00:39:55,768 --> 00:39:58,228
- Who is it? A celebrity? - He's a celebrity.

534
00:39:58,229 --> 00:39:59,688
- Is it Cha Eun Bin? - Yes.

535
00:39:59,689 --> 00:40:02,609
- Celebrities look special indeed. - You saw his face?

536
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:13,036
(Min Seo's mom)

537
00:40:14,579 --> 00:40:15,662
(Calling)

538
00:40:15,663 --> 00:40:21,669
(Incoming call: J)

539
00:40:25,298 --> 00:40:28,343
I'm going to need divine intervention at this point.

540
00:40:34,390 --> 00:40:37,143
(Incoming call: J)

541
00:40:45,276 --> 00:40:48,780
(Incoming call: J)

542
00:40:55,328 --> 00:40:56,788
Are you all right?

543
00:41:02,210 --> 00:41:04,003
You must've been very shaken yesterday.

544
00:41:05,088 --> 00:41:06,880
Your lover is...

545
00:41:06,881 --> 00:41:10,342
passed out with her head in my office toilet.

546
00:41:10,343 --> 00:41:11,719
Come pick her up.

547
00:41:14,889 --> 00:41:17,892
Both of them are an absolute nightmare, darn it.

548
00:41:20,019 --> 00:41:22,563
Jeez, I'm screwed.

549
00:41:27,151 --> 00:41:29,028
Oh, man.

550
00:41:31,781 --> 00:41:33,199
Shoot.

551
00:41:36,119 --> 00:41:37,495
Darn it.

552
00:41:40,957 --> 00:41:42,124
(It's a total misunderstanding.)

553
00:41:42,125 --> 00:41:43,542
(I only called to get the money.)

554
00:41:43,543 --> 00:41:44,585
(Please don't be mad.)

555
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:47,504
Sorry to keep you waiting.

556
00:41:47,505 --> 00:41:48,923
Oh, hello.

557
00:41:49,966 --> 00:41:52,051
- Did you get this for us? - Yes, please have some.

558
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:50,025
We usually swap them out once a month...

559
00:42:50,026 --> 00:42:51,985
or every two weeks if you prefer.

560
00:42:51,986 --> 00:42:56,615
You can select pieces from your favorite artists too.

561
00:42:56,616 --> 00:42:58,533
I'm sure your opinion is the best choice.

562
00:42:58,534 --> 00:42:59,660
Don't say that.

563
00:43:00,578 --> 00:43:01,870
You wanted some art.

564
00:43:01,871 --> 00:43:03,914
I'll go with whatever you say, Captain Park.

565
00:43:03,915 --> 00:43:04,916
Goodness.

566
00:43:05,958 --> 00:43:07,085
Oh, one second.

567
00:43:14,675 --> 00:43:15,676
There.

568
00:43:16,052 --> 00:43:18,261
Do you have any plans after this?

569
00:43:18,262 --> 00:43:19,596
Plans...

570
00:43:19,597 --> 00:43:20,932
Even if I do, I don't.

571
00:43:21,641 --> 00:43:23,642
Then, let me treat you to a meal.

572
00:43:23,643 --> 00:43:26,019
- Do you like eel? - Eel?

573
00:43:26,020 --> 00:43:29,856
There's this spot called King Eel, where I only take special guests.

574
00:43:29,857 --> 00:43:31,441
It's really popular with a long line.

575
00:43:31,442 --> 00:43:32,609
Let's head there right away.

576
00:43:32,610 --> 00:43:35,029
- They always get me a room. - Sounds wonderful.

577
00:43:36,531 --> 00:43:38,032
Shall we go down to the first floor?

578
00:43:39,909 --> 00:43:42,744
She's got to be kidding me.

579
00:43:42,745 --> 00:43:45,581
Special guests, my foot. What a joke.

580
00:43:48,126 --> 00:43:49,335
Anyone in there?

581
00:43:54,132 --> 00:43:55,299
Excuse me?

582
00:44:09,856 --> 00:44:11,273
Oh, boy.

583
00:44:11,274 --> 00:44:13,401
Are you okay?

584
00:44:14,110 --> 00:44:15,361
Are you all right?

585
00:44:17,905 --> 00:44:20,283
- Don't come. - Sorry.

586
00:44:25,580 --> 00:44:26,581
Oh, my.

587
00:44:31,252 --> 00:44:33,171
Are you sure you're okay?

588
00:44:33,713 --> 00:44:35,339
Don't come.

589
00:44:36,174 --> 00:44:37,382
Well...

590
00:44:37,383 --> 00:44:39,760
I'll wait right outside.

591
00:44:52,607 --> 00:44:55,193
(Car Maintenance and Repair Record, Owner: Lim Jae Hong)

592
00:44:57,153 --> 00:44:58,612
Sir.

593
00:44:58,613 --> 00:45:00,906
Are you sure...

594
00:45:00,907 --> 00:45:02,407
the owner is a guy?

595
00:45:02,408 --> 00:45:03,575
Yes.

596
00:45:03,576 --> 00:45:05,410
He's that actor, you know.

597
00:45:05,411 --> 00:45:06,745
- An actor? - The one...

598
00:45:06,746 --> 00:45:09,664
from "Townhouse" or "Model House."

599
00:45:09,665 --> 00:45:11,458
What was his name again?

600
00:45:11,459 --> 00:45:12,709
Oh, one second.

601
00:45:12,710 --> 00:45:15,462
I got an autograph from him. It was Cha something.

602
00:45:15,463 --> 00:45:17,423
Here it is.

603
00:45:18,216 --> 00:45:19,467
Cha Eun Bin.
